.Dd 2026-11-08
.Dt LBTS-TREE 1
.\" Manual page created by:
.\" Guus Sliepen <guus@lightbts.info>
.Sh NAME
.Nm lbts tree
.Nd show tickets and the tickets they link to, recursively
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm lbts tree
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl -link Ar type
.Op Fl -sort Ar field
.Op Fl -depth Ar n
.Op Fl -markdown | Fl -json
.Op Ar id
.Op Ar selector ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The command shows a ticket, the tickets it links to, the tickets those link to, and so on.
By default, it follows
.Ql depends
links, and
.Ql blocks
links in the other direction, since ticket A depends on ticket B if B blocks A.
This makes it possible to keep a roadmap as a ticket that depends on a ticket for each item,
each of which can have items of its own.
.Pp
Without an
.Ar id ,
the trees of all tickets that link to other tickets, but are not linked to themselves, are shown.
Tickets that can only be reached through a cycle of links are shown starting from the one with the lowest number.
.Pp
Each ticket is shown with its number, ID, status and title,
and if it links to other tickets, how many of those are done.
Tickets that are not done are followed by their description.
A ticket that links back to one of the tickets above it is shown as a single line marked
.Ql (see above) .
.Pp
The selectors are those of
.Nm lbts list ,
see
.Xr lbts-fields 5 .
Tickets that don't match them are not shown, nor are the tickets below them.
Unlike
.Nm lbts list ,
tickets of any status are selected by default.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Also show the descriptions of tickets that are done.
.It Fl -link Ar type
Follow links of this type instead of
.Ql depends .
.It Fl -sort Ar field
Sort the tickets below each ticket by a field, as with
.Nm lbts list .
The default is the
.Va cli.sort
configuration variable, or the ticket number.
.It Fl -depth Ar n
Show at most
.Ar n
levels below the given ticket.
.It Fl -markdown
Write Markdown, with a heading for each ticket.
This can be used to generate a roadmap document from the tickets.
.It Fl -json
Write JSON: an object for a ticket, as with
.Ql lbts show --json ,
but with its
.Va description
and with its
.Va children
as an array of the same objects.
Without an
.Ar id ,
an array of these trees.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a roadmap with two items, and show it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
lbts create -m "The plans for the next release." Roadmap
lbts create --link blocks:1 -m "..." First item
lbts create --link blocks:1 -m "..." Second item
lbts tree 1
.Ed
